+# Telegram alert-channel recurrence addendum — #2226 recovery was temporary; finding is intermittent
+
+Task ID: bridge-20261029-telegram2226-recurrence
+Refs: #2226 (original finding; my recovery receipt landed as 0316f41 / PR #2244), #2237 (sentry pass 16 — first re-arm reading 18:44Z), #2212 (original onset sweep + restart precedent), #2268 (same-window PR-plane receipt, independent plane)
+Lane: **report-only addendum to my own receipt.** Zero mutation; zero secret/destructive tools; three zero-credential system_health reads are the entire evidence surface. No new issue filed (zero-duplicate law — #2226 remains the single tracked order for this defect and is still open).
+
+## Why this addendum exists
+
+The #2226 recovery receipt (landed ~3h ago) archived the first outage window (DOWN 17:21:03.648Z → healthy by 18:44Z), bounded the blind spot at ≤1h23m, and closed with an explicit conditional: "no further Render shell diagnostics are required **unless the outage recurs** (if it does, the admin should capture, from inside the container BEFORE any restart: a verbose curl fetch of api.telegram.org plus DNS resolution output)". **It recurred.** At 21:05:39Z the tower vantage reports telegram-primary unreachable again — identical signature, and this time nobody else was watching: the provider sentry passes (#2271 20:49Z, #2274 20:54Z) cover the 7/8 AI-provider set and do not probe the notify plane, so without this addendum the second blind window would have no tracked observation at all.
+
+## The datum: second outage window, same signature
+
+| Time (UTC) | Event | Telegram state | Source |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 17:21:03.648Z | Window 1 onset: `fetch failed` | DOWN | #2212 post-restart sweep |
+| 18:08:49Z | Window 1 confirmed ≥47 min | DOWN | #2226 filing body |
